  "narrative": "Compared to last sale (10-12-26): All feeder cattle were too lightly tested to develop any market trend, however higher undertones were noted. Demand for feeder cattle was mostly moderate for light offerings. Quality this week was mostly plain to average. Most feeders were offered in small packages with many singles noticed. Weigh up cows sold uneven; breaking and lean flesh cows sold 2.00 to 5.00 lower, while boning cows sold 5.00 higher. Weigh up cows sold on moderate to good demand for moderate offerings. Cow quality this week was mixed from plain to average. Feeding cows sold with mostly moderate to good demand. Feeding cows sold mostly steady to 5.00 higher on breaking and boning cows, lean flesh cows sold 3.00 to 5.00 lower. Slaughter bulls sold 3.00 to 4.00 lower. Feeding bulls sold steady to 1.00 lower. Quality was mostly average to attractive this week. Young age cows suitable to feed or rebreed sold on moderate to good demand. Quality this week was mostly average. Steady to higher undertones were noted. Supply included: 44% Feeder Cattle (40% Steers, 56% Heifers, 4% Bulls); 44% Slaughter Cattle (89% Cows, 11% Bulls); 12% Replacement Cattle (81% Stock Cows, 19% Bred Cows). Feeder cattle supply over 600 lbs was 21%.",
